          "note": "Confirmed in 14 national registers so far: Benin, Burkina Faso, Cameroon, DR Congo, Ethiopia, Kenya, Mozambique, Myanmar (2022 renewal list), Nigeria, Rwanda, Senegal, Tanzania, Viet Nam and Zambia. Register detail: Tanzania — 2 registrations (TMDA, issued 8 Mar 2022, Registered/Compliant); Nigeria — granules B4-9425 (NAFDAC Greenbook, approved 28 Feb 2024, Active); Rwanda — tablets and granules (Rwanda FDA, 17 Aug 2024, valid); Zambia — tablets ZAMRA-HM-25-239 (11 Jul 2025, Registered/Compliant); Viet Nam — 2 registrations (DAV, first 27 Dec 2013, valid). MMV and Shin Poong reported in November 2022 that Pyramax was registered in 29 countries in Africa and Asia; that count is the manufacturer's own and has not been checked against national registers. The PYRAPREG trial protocol (BMJ Open, 2023) reports the tablets registered in 19 African and 5 Asian countries, and the granules in 15 African countries",
