          "hasStatus": "launch:status-done",
          "note": "Nine WHO-prequalified presentations from three companies: Alfasigma (2015; requalified 8 and 20 Jan 2025), Guilin (2019–2020, including 3 dispersible) and Beijing Holley (2023). WHO records list one site as the only dihydroartemisinin ingredient source for 8 of the 9.",
          "dateLabel": "2015–2023; requalified Jan 2025",
          "source": "WHO PQ list of prequalified medicines (extract 22 Aug 2026)",
          "asOf": "2026-08-22"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://kochrisdev.github.io/launch-transparency-dashboard/ontology/launch-data.jsonld#product-dhappq-stage-4",
          "@type": "StageEntry",
          "atStage": "launch:stage-4",
          "hasStatus": "launch:status-done",
          "note": "Confirmed in 20 national registers so far: Benin, Burkina Faso, Cameroon, Côte d'Ivoire, DR Congo, Ethiopia, Indonesia, Kenya, Mozambique, Myanmar (2022 renewal list), Namibia, Nigeria, Rwanda, Senegal, Tanzania, Thailand, The Gambia, Viet Nam, Zambia and Zimbabwe. Register detail: Tanzania — 10 presentations across four manufacturers (Guilin D-ARTEPP incl. paediatric dispersible, KBN-Zhejiang Duo-Cotecxin, Ajanta Ridmal), all Registered/Compliant; Nigeria — 47 presentations, of which 25 are active and 22 have lapsed (registrations not being maintained, itself an underuse signal). Since July 2015 Eurartesim has been entrusted exclusively to Pierre Fabre in 32 African countries (Sigma-Tau, now Alfasigma); that is a commercial licence, not a registration, so those countries are not counted here",
          "dateLabel": "2010 (Viet Nam, the earliest registration on the national registers checked); rolling",
          "nextStep": "Verify remaining countries against national registers",
          "nextDate": "TBC",
          "source": "NAFDAC, Rwanda FDA, TMDA, DAV, ZAMRA and MCAZ registers (see the country access map); NAFDAC Greenbook + TMDA IMIS2 extracts 31 Aug 2026; Sigma-Tau and Pierre Fabre, 2 Jul 2015",
          "asOf": "2026-11-03"
        },
